+# Unlock client integration QA (isolated only)
+
+Client implementation: `7a19a18`; reviewed backend: `b8d91c0`. Integration merge `3b50261` is **not a deployment branch**: it includes the backend baseline's old public export. Transfer client and backend changes selectively while preserving the hosted site's current public export and CORS changes.
+
+`node --experimental-strip-types scripts/qa/unlock-contract-fixtures.ts` applies migrations into an isolated PGlite memory database, registers two synthetic accounts and generates actual API response fixtures. It uses no live database URL or production service. `godot --headless --path godot --script res://tests/run_unlock_contract_tests.gd` passes those JSON responses through the real client API decoder/UI with an injected HTTPRequest substitute. This verifies 101 assertions, including all five background codes, duplicate redemption, all eleven reserved hero codes, unknown codes, authentication header construction, ownership restoration through /me, switching accounts, and scrollable layout at four viewport sizes. This is contract integration, not a real network/device end-to-end test.
+
+Reserved codes: W2026 G2026 J2026 B2026 N2026 E2026 JB2026 T2026 JY2026 GM2026 D2026. They grant no hero until the real assets/roster IDs and server hero-selection checks are implemented. The five backgrounds are procedural prototypes. They change no match rules or other player's display.
+
+Cloud visual QA is blocked: the available headless Godot display only supports its dummy renderer. Xorg with a dummy display fails to create local listening sockets, including the approved isolated retry. No Mac GUI was used. A real rendered phone/tablet preview is still required to approve artwork/readability; passing geometry tests is not visual approval. No exports, migration, account unlock, server change or deployment occurred on production.
